Run these commands from the OwnKeep project directory.

```bash
cd /Users/taraka/Taraka/ALVITEQ/flutter/apps/own_keep

# Clean and restore dependencies
flutter clean
flutter pub get

# Validate the project
flutter analyze
flutter test

# Check connected devices
flutter devices

# Run and install debug build on the connected device
flutter run
```

If multiple devices are connected:

```bash
flutter devices
flutter run -d <DEVICE_ID>
```

Build and install APK manually:

```bash
flutter build apk --debug
# Preserve the existing local vault and PIN while updating the debug APK.
adb -s <DEVICE_ID> install -r build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-debug.apk
```

Do not use `flutter install` for OwnKeep development updates. It may uninstall
the existing app first, which permanently deletes the device-local vault, PIN,
preferences, and every document that has not been exported to a backup.

For a release APK after configuring `android/key.properties`:

```bash
flutter build apk --release
adb -s <DEVICE_ID> install -r build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk
```

For the Play Store AAB:

```bash
flutter build appbundle --release
```

Or run the complete release validation:

```bash
./scripts/play_release_preflight.sh
```

Useful maintenance commands:

```bash
# Regenerate localization files
flutter gen-l10n

# Regenerate generated Dart/database code when required
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs

# Show dependency status
flutter pub outdated

# View device logs
flutter logs -d <DEVICE_ID>
```

Recommended full debug sequence:

```bash
cd /Users/taraka/Taraka/ALVITEQ/flutter/apps/own_keep
flutter clean
flutter pub get
flutter gen-l10n
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
flutter analyze
flutter test
flutter devices
flutter run -d <DEVICE_ID>
```
